Consultant: I think we go to movies really to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:11.340
see transformation. Transformation&nbsp;
means that the story had an effect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:15.840
the series of events that you've watched,&nbsp;
it had some consequence it had an effect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.100
on the character that went through them.&nbsp;
That's one reason and then I think also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:26.820
even if nobody talks about it this way,&nbsp;
we look for that transformation as like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:36.300
a inspiration or you could call it a guide for&nbsp;
living a good life. It's this person went through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:44.520
this experience and came out the other side can&nbsp;
give you hope it can give you a little bit of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:50.280
guide guide on how to live and be a better person&nbsp;
but that's like what gives the story meaning in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:58.980
the end how does transformation relate to theme&nbsp;
well I think that most often we see the theme of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:04.320
the movie through the character's transformation&nbsp;
so whatever that lesson is that they learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.400
from going through this whole experience&nbsp;
that's basically the theme of your movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

