the the theme is like the organizing principle&nbsp;
of your story and everything connects to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:22.200
theme and everything falls under the umbrella of&nbsp;
the theme and the way your movie plays out proves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:27.480
the theme to the audience and so a big part of&nbsp;
that is the way the protagonist goes through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:32.880
story and what happens to them how they transform&nbsp;
because of what they've gone through so we see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:38.580
the theme the meaning or that takeaway message&nbsp;
of the story we see that through the way the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:43.920
character transforms most often for some reason&nbsp;
I'm thinking of like Goodwill Hunting just popped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:49.020
into my mind it's been many years since I've seen&nbsp;
it yeah the transformation of that character yeah&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:55.980
and the theme would be what just I know you said&nbsp;
helped earlier yeah well I think that it themes&nbsp;&nbsp;

